  priceLabel: 'Park entry USD 70 to 200 / person / day',
  priceNote: 'Seasonal pricing applies. Peak season (Jul to Oct) USD 200. Low season USD 70. All-inclusive packages from USD 900.',
  intro: [
    'The Masai Mara National Reserve is the most celebrated wildlife destination on Earth. This 1,510 km- reserve in southwestern Kenya forms the northern extension of Tanzania\'s Serengeti ecosystem, and together they host the Great Migration - the annual movement of over 1.5 million wildebeest, 200,000 zebras and 300,000 Thomson\'s gazelles in a continuous circular loop.',
    'Between July and October the wildebeest herds arrive in the Mara from the Serengeti. The Mara River crossings - where enormous herds plunge into crocodile-filled water under the watchful eye of waiting lions and hyenas - are the defining images of African wildlife photography. No two crossings are alike and no crossing is predictable, which is what makes positioning yourself on the banks an exhilarating waiting game.',
    'Outside the migration the Masai Mara consistently produces the finest big cat sightings in Africa. The reserve supports large lion prides, resident cheetah families and numerous leopards. The open savannah grassland makes vehicle-based observation easier than almost anywhere else in East Africa.',
