const sections = [];
const faqs = [
  { q: 'When do the wildebeest arrive in the Masai Mara?', a: 'The wildebeest herds typically begin arriving in the Masai Mara from late June or early July and remain until October. Peak Mara River crossing activity is generally in August and September. The exact timing varies by year and rainfall patterns in the Serengeti. The herds begin moving back south in late October and November.' },
  { q: 'Is a hot air balloon safari worth the cost?', a: 'Most guests who do the balloon safari rate it as the highlight of their Kenya trip. The predawn launch, the silence over the savannah at sunrise and the aerial perspective on the herds of game below are genuinely extraordinary. It costs approximately USD 480 per person and needs to be booked in advance.' },
  { q: 'What is the difference between the Masai Mara National Reserve and the Mara Triangle?', a: 'The Masai Mara National Reserve is managed by the Narok County Council. The Mara Triangle is the western portion managed by the Mara Conservancy - a private non-profit. The Mara Triangle is generally considered better managed, less crowded and has more reliable river crossing positions. Some premium camps are located there and include the higher conservation fee in their rates.' },
